{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony","id":96423,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Harmony","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-22T11:03:16-07:00","id":96423,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Harmony","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> Since Stew has been giving us weekly votes to see which aspect of the upcoming Werewolf rework we want to learn about, I thought this would be a good place to discuss reactions, questions, concerns, benefits, and so on of the current revealed topic.<br /> <br /> My personal option with the new Harmony system is <b>HELL YES!</b><br /> <br /> What I really love about the new Harmony system is that Werewolves were always an experience sponge. You could throw hundreds of experience into them for little benefit before simply due to the massive amount of stuff they could purchase. With Harmony out of the experience picture, it gives players an opportunity for serious roleplay without the nagging thought of experience on their mind. Before, while I may want to try playing a Werewolf who lives to destroy the pure out of revenge for his dead pack, as a player, I knew that it was a 1 way trip down experience hell if I ever wanted to raise it again.<br /> <br /> Now, while there are obviously certain breaking points which we are unaware of yet, the simple fact that experience is no longer the deciding factor in raising or lowing it provides a far richer environment with which to work in.<br /> <br /> This, and the fact that rituals are no longer paired with Harmony opens the floor greatly to their use for all werewolves and not just the ones with high Harmony","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T11:26:09-07:00","id":96436,"title":"","content":"I totally agree with you my friend , This the first actual fact we see about this new wonderful-to-be-book . It will possibly be the best werewolf book EVER . I love the idea of harmony as a balance factor free from experience ponts . There will be a challenge I believe with the breaking points that will increase or decrease the base harmony level , which will be 5 . My players are spirit wolf style \u03bf\u03bd\u03b5\u03c3 , so I believe they will never care about 5-10 harmony ,mostly they will keep 5-4 keeping an eye not to drop further .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 03-22-2014, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T11:43:24-07:00","id":96447,"title":"","content":"This is a huge step towards making Forsakem the game I've always wanted it to be, but never really felt it played like. Obviously a lot will depend on the specific Breaking Points, but since they're customizable I'm not too worried about that. Personally, my favorite part is the consequences of having your Harmony too high or to low. Before, the Spirit Cop game was the only way to play (that was supported by the mechanics, anyway). But with Harmony affecting your Death Rage Conditions, your Bans, and your ability to shapeshift, it sounds like you will be able to capture the feel of the classic Wolfman story just by playing a low Harmony character. Or you can crank up the spirit world side of things even more by playing a high Harmony one. And since it slides both ways by breaking points, you can safely experiment with your character moving more towards one side or the other without fear of having to pay Experiences to adjust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T13:05:41-07:00","id":96498,"title":"","content":"Obviously the breaking parts will be a huge part of it and the optimist in my wants to have confidence in them to provide a fun gameplay experience regardless of the path you choose to take...flesh or spirit. Certain mechanics based upon Harmony are obviously really useful such as reflexive and dice free shapeshifting sound massively appealing and help keep the role-play element of being a fur covered war machine alive.<br /> <br /> Now obviously if I learn more towards the human side of things, I <b>WANT</b> the penalty to shapeshift as it can add the roleplay aspect of suppressing the wolf side to my character should I wish to do so. Perhaps my character gave in to the wolf too much one day and his best friend was killed as a result. Now, I want to toss away that heritage and try to live as a normal human. On the flip side, perhaps I was too focused on being human and neglected the spirit side of things. Suddenly, my entire life, family, and friends are in danger from spiritual predation and I have no way to fight back without sacrificing the last 15 years of my life's work. The possibilities are endless when experience isn't involved to limit you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T13:23:04-07:00","id":96506,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea that it's a sliding scale with the middle being the best spot to be. Though I think it would be served better as a concept with having there be +5 harmony for too human and -5 harmony for too wolf to make it clear they are extremes and the morality chart is not a straight procession.<br /> <br /> Like I have said before, I've encountered a lot of people playing their uratha as essentially human (heck, some books paint them as way too human). Having there be clear disadvantages to being too human (Ian said it well in the blog; you become the movie monster) really helps to bring fort that Uratha are not simply humans who shift, but creatures of both worlds who must balance them. I'd actually think this kind of morality chrt would be great for WtA as well.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I guess my only worry is, that the wolf aspect might again be snuffed in favour of the spirit. Hopefully, that is not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-22-2014, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T13:35:28-07:00","id":96510,"title":"","content":"Hm, I know I voted Woldblooded for the net article, but I'm wondering if there are any particular trends, Harmony-wise, amongst the Tribes? Will some tribes tend to favour or look down on higher or lower Harmony werewolves? Not necessarily zealously, but as a consequence of their preferences","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T13:57:43-07:00","id":96522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=96510#post96510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I know I voted Woldblooded for the net article, but I'm wondering if there are any particular trends, Harmony-wise, amongst the Tribes? Will some tribes tend to favour or look down on higher or lower Harmony werewolves? Not necessarily zealously, but as a consequence of their preferences</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I'm wondering where the multiple PU7+ Harmony 8+ Meninna on the books would fall on the new scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T14:21:07-07:00","id":96537,"title":"","content":"One thing that fascinates me is the idea of how involved Harmony shifts are. While it's always been thematically okay to raise a Morality/Integrity Stat if it was appropriate, a lot of it came down to exp expenditure, as mentioned in the first post. Now, rises and falls are regular things that are evoked by neither EXP nor big moments, but the regular activities of the players, making it more alive and vivid and involved in PC lives. Add in the idea of just how hard they're implying it is for a stat to stay in place, and it creates the impression that being a werewolf is like living in a endless storm-which is a metaphor I can completely get behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T15:08:10-07:00","id":96554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=96522#post96522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm wondering where the multiple PU7+ Harmony 8+ Meninna on the books would fall on the new scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am wondering this as well, since under current mechanics, at that level of PU, you need to spend a ton of time in the Shadow. As a werewolf with high Harmony towards human, this may be all but impossible.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it is reversed depending on your Harmony? Then again, it wouldn't work upon further thought as it currently is written. What if I am a PU6 werewolf with Harmony 10? I need to spend time in the Shadow to prevent essence bleed, but can't step foot in the Shadow. I guess it is something we will just need to wait and find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T21:34:31-07:00","id":96711,"title":"","content":"I'm picturing The Wolf of the Woods being on Harmony 4 per the new system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T01:00:10-07:00","id":96770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=96554#post96554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am wondering this as well, since under current mechanics, at that level of PU, you need to spend a ton of time in the Shadow. As a werewolf with high Harmony towards human, this may be all but impossible.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it is reversed depending on your Harmony? Then again, it wouldn't work upon further thought as it currently is written. What if I am a PU6 werewolf with Harmony 10? I need to spend time in the Shadow to prevent essence bleed, but can't step foot in the Shadow. I guess it is something we will just need to wait and find out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe High PU on the high Harmony side doesn't involve living in the Shadow or essence bleed as we know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T05:06:33-07:00","id":96826,"title":"","content":"Well, obviously the new Harmony means something a bit different to the old, so an existing character with Harmony 8+ will need to be heavily reassessed. Depending on the character's nature, I'd hazard a guess that they'll be in the 4-6 band of Harmony - for now, at least.<br /> <br /> Primal Urge, well, you'll have to wait and see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A nice thing about the new Harmony system is that it can actually encourage quite extreme acts to get yourself back into balance. You're a starting Uratha at Harmony 7, want to get to Harmony 5 and, oh, since you're new you're running low on Essence fast? Try new the new HarmonyDown! (tm) diet, made of 100% eating people!<br /> <br /> (note, I haven't actually checked whether eating people is a Harmony Breaking Point and, if so, where it is on the chart, this is just me assuming)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T09:45:23-07:00","id":96924,"title":"","content":"I hope from a personal standpoint that some of the acts required to have a high harmony and some that give you a low harmony are changed around a bit. Slaying a werewolf in the heat of battle was always a bit of an annoyance for me from a thematic standpoint since it essentially meant that if I have a pack of high harmony uratha, and they are constantly under attack, they have no long term solution to fix the problem besides moving. This 1 particular harmony level gave an enormous advantage to the Pure who were willing to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T10:55:50-07:00","id":96945,"title":"","content":"I hope (and I'm fairly confident, knowing a little about Stew's preferences) that killing other werewolves remains a breaking point. Fighting the Pure isn't supposed to be easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T11:44:00-07:00","id":96971,"title":"","content":"I think killing in general posses an interesting issue with the new Harmony concept. Killing is not a uniquely &quot;human&quot; or &quot;spirit&quot; action. It seems like killing becomes a very situational issue for Harmony where making it always a breaking point to kill another werewolf is going to be very hard to slot in. Though I guess there's also the lingering question of when do actions that promote the flesh and the spirit cancel each other out for no breaking point, and when do you end up rolling a breaking point in each direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T12:46:12-07:00","id":96998,"title":"","content":"Hmm, interesting point... It seems like a fair bit does ride on just what exactly the Harmony Breaking Points are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T12:46:16-07:00","id":96999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=96945#post96945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope (and I'm fairly confident, knowing a little about Stew's preferences) that killing other werewolves remains a breaking point. Fighting the Pure isn't supposed to be easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing someone can totally still be a breaking point, but I think the WAY you kill that person is important. If you kill with your claws or teeth, for example, that's a very vivid, very memorable reminder that you're not human, and you might slip toward the spirit side of your being. Blowing someone away with a shotgun because he scammed you in an investment scheme, that's going to push you toward the human side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T15:16:08-07:00","id":97071,"title":"","content":"Nevermind that retaining some manner of balance is an active thing - so if you slip on either side of the scales by murdering Pure, it's much easier to try to correct your balance than to try to hoard say, 21xp points to buy Harmony 7 once again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T16:34:08-07:00","id":97120,"title":"","content":"While true, even if Harmony wasn't being redone to reflect a balancing act ~5 instead of the higher the better, the GMC era rules updates already took some serious steps towards not having trying to maintain a higher level be quite so frustrating. Even taking the old concept of Harmony and converting it to follow either the new Integrity or the new Humanity would have reduced that frustration considerably.<br /> <br /> It does make me wonder a bit how XP either directly, or indirectly through Merits and the like, will impact the new Harmony setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T19:39:11-07:00","id":97217,"title":"","content":"Well...only time will tell. Regardless, simply freeing Uratha from that experience investiture is already a major boon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T20:20:32-07:00","id":97238,"title":"","content":"In a sense, you'll be constantly hunting for your own self-balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T20:39:00-07:00","id":97251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=97238#post97238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a sense, you'll be constantly hunting for your own self-balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you did there.<br /> <br /> I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T00:45:11-07:00","id":97349,"title":"","content":"Horizontally placed was how I saw it as well; it's an easy visual slider that way without it overtly seeming like one side is the &quot;top&quot; and the other the &quot;bottom&quot;. May take a bit of a sheet shuffling in format, but it wouldn't be too hard to place it in that style above and below Willpower and Essence with a tick on the sweet spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T01:17:00-07:00","id":97359,"title":"","content":"Given the general layout of nWOD sheets, I'm not sure horizontal would work well. On top of that, the current layout vertically leaves room for text next to each level of Harmony. Keeping it this way gives you space to note the effects of each level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:19:35-07:00","id":97394,"title":"","content":"I don't see the issue with it not being able to be horizontal if it were actually to be - Mr Gone pretty much is a wizard at sheets, just get him to do it!<br /> <br /> I very much like where Harmony is going.<br /> <br /> It has me wondering if it will effect (bonuses etc) for such things as staying in Garou, silver damage, ability to cross gauntlet, has Harmony fluctuates.<br /> <br /> I think someone said on the previous page about making sure that the &quot;wolf&quot; doesn't get left out. Considering Stew has said that it will have a heavy emphasis on &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot; I think that would probably be very much taken into consideration, and I'd be intrigued to see how. For instance, would there be more emphasis on Wolf+Man+Spirit, or would it go more Wolf-Spirt+Man, if that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T02:34:06-07:00","id":97402,"title":"","content":"I'm sure Mr. Gone could get a sheet to work with Harmony done horizontally. I'm not sure how it would look aesthetically though. And I think the concept of keeping horizontal lines next to the vertical scale is going to, from a practical perspective, be more important than getting rid of a &quot;up = good, down = bad,&quot; bias. Especially because the game already has a &quot;right = good, left = bad&quot; bias on the sheets anyway.<br /> <br /> I'm also pretty sure that Harmony is going to reflect a Wolf-Spirit vs Man design. The Wolf vs Man vs Spirit angle would be a lot of effort to squeeze into one rating and be functional in play. It also makes using the new Harmony model for non-Uratha shapeshifters easier because all you need to do is alter the breaking points for being too spirit like to reflect the spirits of the new animal in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T03:20:25-07:00","id":97426,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure you're right that they'll stick to Wolf-Spirt vs Man. I don't think it wouldn't be functional the other way, but I think it would complicate things unnecessarily. That being said, if there's a part of Harmony where you're really lacking the spirit side of yourself and you end up an uncontrollable slavering wolf beast during your respective moon cycle then that kind of nails it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T23:48:22-07:00","id":98158,"title":"","content":"I love the new Harmony rule and I am half-tempted to come up with my own Breaking Points just so that I can use it now haha. I voted Tribe because - as others have stated - that is one part of W:tF that seems most disconnected with the day to day activity of being Uratha. Sure it brought with it philosophy and attitude and of course some Gifts, but little else. In fact as long as I've played and ST'd W:tF, few players have ever spent much time even thinking about their Tribe. I try my best, having taken inspiration from Mr. Shopping's fantastic Actual Plays, but it needs work.<br /> <br /> Some above have asked for W:tF sheet with horizontal Harmony. Here's mine, using GMC mechanics, heavily based on Mr. Gone's work with Pendragon's house rules for Forms.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.4shared.com/office/HYlzlHCnce/WtF-CharacterSheet_GMC.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.4shared.com/office/HYlzlH...Sheet_GMC.html</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T23:56:25-07:00","id":98162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xaielao</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=98158#post98158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the new Harmony rule and I am half-tempted to come up with my own Breaking Points just so that I can use it now haha. I voted Tribe because - as others have stated - that is one part of W:tF that seems most disconnected with the day to day activity of being Uratha. Sure it brought with it philosophy and attitude and of course some Gifts, but little else. In fact as long as I've played and ST'd W:tF, few players have ever spent much time even thinking about their Tribe. I try my best, having taken inspiration from Mr. Shopping's fantastic Actual Plays, but it needs work.<br /> <br /> Some above have asked for W:tF sheet with horizontal Harmony. Here's mine, using GMC mechanics, heavily based on Mr. Gone's work with Pendragon's house rules for Forms.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.4shared.com/office/HYlzlHCnce/WtF-CharacterSheet_GMC.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.4shared.com/office/HYlzlH...Sheet_GMC.html</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Lota... Lota piracy going on on that site you linked to there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T09:12:09-07:00","id":99216,"title":"","content":"So, Harmony. <br /> <br /> My only worry is that its still going to include a list of spirit bans on at least one side of the issue. I really hope that its something much more to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T09:46:10-07:00","id":99242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=99216#post99216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Harmony.<br /> <br /> My only worry is that its still going to include a list of spirit bans on at least one side of the issue. I really hope that its something much more to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was stated that leaning more towards the spirit side of Harmony will result in the taking of bans. Actually, I really liked that aspect as it is currently and hope it stays similar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T14:09:47-07:00","id":99494,"title":"","content":"Well, it had to happen sooner or later.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> With all this positive feedback about Harmony, it really pains me to be &quot;that guy&quot;, so I'm sorry about this. I'll be honest, I'm not sure if I like what I'm seeing. At first I thought it was pretty cool, but now that I've sat on it for the past few days I'm starting to have my doubts. What it's starting to look like to me is a glorified speedometer, &quot; Oops, I'm going too Spirit. I need to speed up more. Oops, I'm going to Human. I need to slow down a bit&quot;. IMHO, this makes Werewolves more complicated to play then they need to be.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure I like shapeshifting being tied to Harmony as presented. I mean, it does make sense but with Harmony constantly jumping back and forth like Stew is saying, it means more book keeping than shapeshifting needs. A simple mechanic is being made more complicated.<br /> <br /> I don't know. Maybe I'm just being paranoid. It might not be as bad as I'm thinking. I'll wait until the final product to make my final verdict. Again, sorry for being a downer, guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T14:29:20-07:00","id":99503,"title":"","content":"Personally I think the approach is solid gold, though I agree that they need to be careful with shape-shifting rolls. I've literally never encountered a scenario where such a roll did anything but slowdown the game and frustrate the player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T14:47:46-07:00","id":99516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=99494#post99494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it had to happen sooner or later.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> With all this positive feedback about Harmony, it really pains me to be &quot;that guy&quot;, so I'm sorry about this. I'll be honest, I'm not sure if I like what I'm seeing. At first I thought it was pretty cool, but now that I've sat on it for the past few days I'm starting to have my doubts. What it's starting to look like to me is a glorified speedometer, &quot; Oops, I'm going too Spirit. I need to speed up more. Oops, I'm going to Human. I need to slow down a bit&quot;. IMHO, this makes Werewolves more complicated to play then they need to be.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure I like shapeshifting being tied to Harmony as presented. I mean, it does make sense but with Harmony constantly jumping back and forth like Stew is saying, it means more book keeping than shapeshifting needs. A simple mechanic is being made more complicated.<br /> <br /> I don't know. Maybe I'm just being paranoid. It might not be as bad as I'm thinking. I'll wait until the final product to make my final verdict. Again, sorry for being a downer, guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a valid point, and a lot of our speculation is simply that...speculation. The problem is we don't have solid rules in front of us right now so it may be solid gold, or it could be the shits. What I feel it comes down to is exactly which mechanics are tied to which level of Harmony, and what the breaking points are going to be. Still, I feel from the information we have gleaned that it will significantly speed up things in most cases as the vast majority of the Uratha should be able to shapeshift in normal circumstances without a roll. It is only at the sweet spot that it becomes no role AND reflexive. At Harmony 4 or 6, it may still be no role, simply an instant action which is still extremely good.<br /> <br /> Again, those benefits are based upon assumptions from the post by Stew, but it seems logical","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:47:15-07:00","id":99666,"title":"","content":"I'd expect modifiers (dice bonuses or penalties) to things like Rituals (which is not the same as outright rolling the Harmony for those) or Shapeshifting the closer one stays on balance or not. I don't think it would be too hard to keep track off. Heck, why shouldn't some rites rely more on the flesh than the spirit, for example? Lots and lots of design space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T20:53:16-07:00","id":99709,"title":"","content":"One thing I am wondering about is how the new Harmony will interact with other powers that use a target's Integrity trait in some way. For example, like some Lucifuge Castigations or demonic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T04:50:28-07:00","id":99922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=99242#post99242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it was stated that leaning more towards the spirit side of Harmony will result in the taking of bans. Actually, I really liked that aspect as it is currently and hope it stays similar.</div> </div> </div> </div> The old Harmony was effectively a list of spirit bans that, if you broke it, you developed different spirit bans. It didn't have much to do with balancing man and wolf. And it came with some rather unfortunate implications as well.<br /> <br /> We know that its going to be balancing man with -something- now. Is it going to be a wolf... or a spirit? They say spirit-wolf, but which is going to be the focus? Is it still going to feel more like a bans and spiritual laws than something more organic / natural? <br /> <br /> That's my worry. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">One thing I am wondering about is how the new Harmony will interact with other powers that use a target's Integrity trait in some way. For example, like some Lucifuge Castigations or demonic powers.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> I'd imagine that, since lucifuge/infernal powers are mainly a Hunter thing, the new Hunter book that has some updates will cover that.</span> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T09:53:18-07:00","id":100114,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking that a werewolf's Gauru form might change in certain purely-aesthetic ways to reflect their Harmony score. Go too far toward the human side and your war-form will have a more humanoid appearance; go too far to spirit and you'll look more bestial, perhaps even going on all fours in a few cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T10:45:06-07:00","id":100159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=99922#post99922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The old Harmony was effectively a list of spirit bans that, if you broke it, you developed different spirit bans. It didn't have much to do with balancing man and wolf. And it came with some rather unfortunate implications as well.<br /> <br /> We know that its going to be balancing man with -something- now. Is it going to be a wolf... or a spirit? They say spirit-wolf, but which is going to be the focus? Is it still going to feel more like a bans and spiritual laws than something more organic / natural?<br /> <br /> That's my worry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, while what you said was technically true as to how Harmony and spirit bans manifested in regards to balancing man and wolf, I still felt it was a fun mechanic to deal with. Technically, it started showcasing what happens when a Werewolf becomes too much towards spirit. Any good mechanic in the future should hopefully create a fun experience regardless of what it actually does rather than feel like a penalty for not playing a specific way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T14:35:12-07:00","id":100348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=99922#post99922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The old Harmony was effectively a list of spirit bans that, if you broke it, you developed different spirit bans. It didn't have much to do with balancing man and wolf. And it came with some rather unfortunate implications as well.<br /> <br /> We know that its going to be balancing man with -something- now. Is it going to be a wolf... or a spirit? They say spirit-wolf, but which is going to be the focus? Is it still going to feel more like a bans and spiritual laws than something more organic / natural?<br /> <br /> That's my worry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I share your worry. Some books had the NPCs basically be shamans instead of werewolves, since the focus was on spirit vs man more than the wolf. Its an easy thing to mess up,too, as the game material supports that balance much more than the wolf vs man.<br /> <br /> However, I like the new Harmony much more when it comes to the Pure. In the old, I always felt the Harmony was rather silly when it came to the Pure, as OBVIOUSLY they were wrong as the morality chart said so. Now, it isn't at all so clear and the Pure can easily be at any point in the scale, taking away the certainty of the old Harmony and replacing it with the much murkier new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:03:31-07:00","id":100371,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the old Harmony Chart would have been far less an issue if it wasn't a redux of the Oath of the Moon overall; it seemed very, very odd that the Meta-mechanic clicked precisely with an IC abstract on such a one for one basis. Some references made sense, but basically having a shopping list Oath that ever so neatly played along with your Harmony mechanic was really off in my eyes, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Too clean, too neat, too precise. There really wasn't much wiggle room or room for interpretation that didn't just bork your Harmony (which made many so-called Blasphemies a nice idea in theory, but really not applicable in practice), and it got even odder with the Pure involved (see the Predator Kings for a good example, and having to backport notions of Dire Wolf's rage into it to work around it while justifying why the Tribe was just fucked Harmony wise overall).<br /> <br /> I doubt this is going to be an issue anymore, but really we need to see the &quot;Breaking Points&quot; or Disharmony points or whatever they get called before worrying if it's too much Spirit vs Man and not enough Wolf; we don't see references to that -yet-, but no doubt it's being addressed somehow. I'm just hoping the &quot;going wolf-like means going really spirit-like&quot; possibility isn't the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:34:56-07:00","id":100404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=100371#post100371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the old Harmony Chart would have been far less an issue if it wasn't a redux of the Oath of the Moon overall; it seemed very, very odd that the Meta-mechanic clicked precisely with an IC abstract on such a one for one basis. Some references made sense, but basically having a shopping list Oath that ever so neatly played along with your Harmony mechanic was really off in my eyes, to say the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. When you have something like the Oath, or in WtA, Litany, it should never be tied to the Morality Chart if you have one. Every tribe no doubt has their own take, and having it ruined by basically having your entire morality go against it...yeah. Ambigiousness is the best.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:58:37-07:00","id":100423,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I expect Harmony to focus on the flesh vs. spirit dichotomy and wolf to not really enter into the equation. The man vs. wolf dichotomy will show up in other places. As a werewolf, you will be a human/wolf hybrid no matter where you lie on the Harmony scale, the question is just wether you will be more of a human/wolf hybrid, or more of a spirit-man/spirit-wolf hybrid. And I for one love the idea of playing a character that's really far to the flesh side. How much you focus on the man vs. the wolf will probably come up in other places, such as Primal Urge and probably certain powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:16:52-07:00","id":100445,"title":"","content":"That's what I'm hoping for, personally. As is, there's so many places and so much room to emphasize the Wolf vs Man aspect, I'm not worried if it's not Harmony that's handling that if it's addressed elsewhere. I'm thinking it's likely in Primal Urge myself as well, or perhaps the equivalent of Vice/Virtue/Mask/Dirge areas as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:19:49-07:00","id":100450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=100371#post100371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the old Harmony Chart would have been far less an issue if it wasn't a redux of the Oath of the Moon overall; it seemed very, very odd that the Meta-mechanic clicked precisely with an IC abstract on such a one for one basis. Some references made sense, but basically having a shopping list Oath that ever so neatly played along with your Harmony mechanic was really off in my eyes, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Too clean, too neat, too precise. There really wasn't much wiggle room or room for interpretation that didn't just bork your Harmony (which made many so-called Blasphemies a nice idea in theory, but really not applicable in practice), and it got even odder with the Pure involved (see the Predator Kings for a good example, and having to backport notions of Dire Wolf's rage into it to work around it while justifying why the Tribe was just fucked Harmony wise overall).</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap, this post is beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T12:20:16-07:00","id":100826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony#post96423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> Since Stew has been giving us weekly votes to see which aspect of the upcoming Werewolf rework we want to learn about, I thought this would be a good place to discuss reactions, questions, concerns, benefits, and so on of the current revealed topic.<br /> <br /> My personal option with the new Harmony system is <b>HELL YES!</b><br /> <br /> What I really love about the new Harmony system is that Werewolves were always an experience sponge. You could throw hundreds of experience into them for little benefit before simply due to the massive amount of stuff they could purchase. With Harmony out of the experience picture, it gives players an opportunity for serious roleplay without the nagging thought of experience on their mind. Before, while I may want to try playing a Werewolf who lives to destroy the pure out of revenge for his dead pack, as a player, I knew that it was a 1 way trip down experience hell if I ever wanted to raise it again.<br /> <br /> Now, while there are obviously certain breaking points which we are unaware of yet, the simple fact that experience is no longer the deciding factor in raising or lowing it provides a far richer environment with which to work in.<br /> <br /> This, and the fact that rituals are no longer paired with Harmony opens the floor greatly to their use for all werewolves and not just the ones with high Harmony</div> </div> </div> </div>Could anyone post the link to where the new Harmony system was explained? Thank you<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T12:43:07-07:00","id":100835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/one-foot-in-flesh-and-one-in-spirit/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/one-foot-in-flesh-and-one-in-spirit/\" target=\"_blank\"> One Foot in Flesh and One in Spirit &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/one-foot-in-flesh-and-one-in-spirit/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/one-foot-in-flesh-and-one-in-spirit/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T15:58:52-07:00","id":100924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=100371#post100371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the old Harmony Chart would have been far less an issue if it wasn't a redux of the Oath of the Moon overall; it seemed very, very odd that the Meta-mechanic clicked precisely with an IC abstract on such a one for one basis. Some references made sense, but basically having a shopping list Oath that ever so neatly played along with your Harmony mechanic was really off in my eyes, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Too clean, too neat, too precise. There really wasn't much wiggle room or room for interpretation that didn't just bork your Harmony (which made many so-called Blasphemies a nice idea in theory, but really not applicable in practice), and it got even odder with the Pure involved (see the Predator Kings for a good example, and having to backport notions of Dire Wolf's rage into it to work around it while justifying why the Tribe was just fucked Harmony wise overall).<br /> <br /> I doubt this is going to be an issue anymore, but really we need to see the &quot;Breaking Points&quot; or Disharmony points or whatever they get called before worrying if it's too much Spirit vs Man and not enough Wolf; we don't see references to that -yet-, but no doubt it's being addressed somehow. I'm just hoping the &quot;going wolf-like means going really spirit-like&quot; possibility isn't the case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This was always my biggest issue with it as well. Especially the lower rungs of old!Harmony, the only way to risk those breaks was the ST forcing a scenario. &quot;Oh, so the worst thing is eating the flesh of others? I will almost never run that risk, so no problem!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T17:11:45-07:00","id":100969,"title":"","content":"amaterasu: No PC of yours ever swallowed what he shouldn't in the throes of Kuruth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T17:16:34-07:00","id":100973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=100969#post100969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">amaterasu: No PC of yours ever swallowed what he shouldn't in the throes of Kuruth?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did that crap all the time, especially if I was in Kuruth and low on essence. Always felt guilty afterwards especially since it tasted so good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T22:13:02-07:00","id":101086,"title":"","content":"My main concern with this new scale is the implication that Flesh = Human and Spirit = Wolf. I personally prefer the view that the Wolf is primarily a creature of the flesh, and that the <i>Man</i> is what introduces spirituality into the picture. That said, I definitely like the \u201cbalanced in the middle; opposite kinds of imbalance at the extremes\u201d model being used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T22:22:27-07:00","id":101090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101086#post101086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main concern with this new scale is the implication that Flesh = Human and Spirit = Wolf. I personally prefer the view that the Wolf is primarily a creature of the flesh, and that the <i>Man</i> is what introduces spirituality into the picture. That said, I definitely like the \u201cbalanced in the middle; opposite kinds of imbalance at the extremes\u201d model being used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to confound the issue, but like everything else in life, both wolf and man have been used to express the extremes of flesh and spirit. Wolves have been understood as just eat, breed, and survive as much as they have been seen as being a wise one of the wild, an extremely intelligent being who's still far more inherently understands the natural laws than man with it's specific understanding(like the products of science) can. Like wise, humans have been indulgent, base, and unnecessarily cruel, but also have a level of expression for spirituality that, if nothing else, at least implies a greater spiritual high.<br /> <br /> But let's be honest , trying to map that out accurately invites a DnD grid, and no one wants that. &quot;I whip out my Spiritual Man Werewolf, and use Detect Flesh to find the Bale Hound&quot;.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it may be a little too simplistic, but given that werewolves had identified as human for so long, it feels comfortable enough to say that when the spirit is neglected, the human side prevails. The scale's fine as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-29-2014, 01:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T22:35:53-07:00","id":101098,"title":"","content":"Humanity's lack of spiritual presence has been a thing in the setting for long enough that even if &quot;higher Integrity-equivalent means closer inhabitation of the world humans live in&quot; didn't appear to be a trend it wouldn't make a great deal of sense to put the thing that actually has a spiritual reflection on the opposite side of the scale from the end that trends spirity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T23:33:55-07:00","id":101109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101086#post101086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main concern with this new scale is the implication that Flesh = Human and Spirit = Wolf. I personally prefer the view that the Wolf is primarily a creature of the flesh, and that the <i>Man</i> is what introduces spirituality into the picture. That said, I definitely like the \u201cbalanced in the middle; opposite kinds of imbalance at the extremes\u201d model being used.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, I don't think you'll have to worry too much about this. From what I was reading, it sounds like on the &quot;too flesh&quot; side you'll be part flesh man and part flesh wolf. On the &quot;top spirit&quot; side, you'll be part spirit man and part spirit wolf. Around the middle, you'll be part man and part wolf, both with a relative balance between spirit and flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T01:25:07-07:00","id":101134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=100969#post100969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">amaterasu: No PC of yours ever swallowed what he shouldn't in the throes of Kuruth?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the ST setting up a situation in which it happens. And no, they don't tend to do the &quot;Oh, and I also tear out a chunk and eat it while I'm at it&quot; in that situation.<br /> <br /> There's no game benefit to risking the lower end &quot;sins&quot;. Even gaining 1 Essence for cannibalism isn't much of a reward, unless circumstances force it as a last resort, but again, ST forcing a situation.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, Diablerie is a risk but one that has rewards. There's a cost-benefit analysis that can be done, and the reward lasts long enough to regain the lost Humanity involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd much rather see a gray area, or some complications, or direct conflict where the Oath says &quot;do this&quot; but keeping Harmony in balance you have to not do that, or not as often as you should, or whatever, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:32:01-07:00","id":101283,"title":"","content":"The thing is that while in Kuruth, you don't carefully measure the pros and cons of devouring your prey. And you seem to think that you'd only take 1 essence per turn? Hell, if my Gauru scored 4L worth of a bite, he's getting 4 essence the (reflexive) second he swallows it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:53:10-07:00","id":101301,"title":"","content":"The more I think about the new Harmony, I have to admit, the less I like it. I think it adds a level of complexity that doesn't suit my tastes - two different ways of &quot;falling from grace&quot;, each with their own subsystems that, it seems, affect a character's effectivity quite a bit - your Harmony rating apparently directly affects your ability to shapeshift.<br /> <br /> I like to keep things simpler than that, really; and besides that, the conflict between spirit and flesh is a thing I prefer to explore externally, and not in the context of a werewolf's soul.<br /> <br /> I like the existing Harmony precisely *because* a low Harmony rating doesn't immediately tell you what's wrong - a low Harmony werewolf could be either too human or too spirit-like (or too wolfy - where's the wolf in the new Harmony model? Being a wolf is not the same as being a spirit). That sort of thing is up to the storyteller and the player, just as I like it.<br /> <br /> Still, with what little we know, it's way too early to judge. I remain optimistic. This is Werewolf, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 03-29-2014, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:03:20-07:00","id":101342,"title":"","content":"Well, why wouldn't it affect your ability to shapeshift? I actually think it is one of the most realistic aspects of the new Harmony system. If you try too much to be human, you mentally block yourself from embracing the wolf/spirit side. On the other hand, if you are determined to live your life as a wolf with 1 foot entrenched as a beast, and the other in shadow, why would you ever shift back to human?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I was never really a fan of the old Harmony system for a few reasons mostly because it was extremely easy to abuse at certain levels. Needlessly killing a human a problem? Entice them to attack your pack or a loved one, or someone you value highly. Now you can defend them with no issues at all or Harmony loss. It doesn't matter that you instigated it, since the end result is protection of pack or family which is no longer needless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:25:01-07:00","id":101353,"title":"","content":"I actually missed the Apocalypse old days of &quot;losing the wolf&quot; which is basically what happens when you get too high in Harmony.<br /> <br /> In another of my speculations, I think cannibalism (eating man/wolf/Uratha) would degenerate you downwards, towards the spirit side. Why? because it's what every spirit does - they cannibalize eachother and get essence from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:45:14-07:00","id":101364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101342#post101342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, why wouldn't it affect your ability to shapeshift? I actually think it is one of the most realistic aspects of the new Harmony system.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're aware you're using the term &quot;realistic&quot; in the context of a fictional moral scale of fictional beings based on mythology?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101342#post101342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you try too much to be human, you mentally block yourself from embracing the wolf/spirit side. On the other hand, if you are determined to live your life as a wolf with 1 foot entrenched as a beast, and the other in shadow, why would you ever shift back to human?</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not at all how new Harmony works.<br /> <br /> &quot;At Harmony 10, you can\u2019t enter the Shadow and you need to burn Essence to shapeshift at all (except when you enter Kuruth). At Harmony 0, you\u2019re trapped in the Shadow. You need to spend Essence and roll to <i>not</i> shapeshift when you face an emotional stimulus \u2014 and you\u2019re laden with spirit bans over and above those from totem and lodge.&quot;<br /> <br /> Besides that - can't argue with your preferences; I still have mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101342#post101342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I was never really a fan of the old Harmony system for a few reasons mostly because it was extremely easy to abuse at certain levels. Needlessly killing a human a problem? Entice them to attack your pack or a loved one, or someone you value highly. Now you can defend them with no issues at all or Harmony loss. It doesn't matter that you instigated it, since the end result is protection of pack or family which is no longer needless.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a problem with Harmony, that's a problem with the storyteller not really understanding Harmony as a setting concept and game mechanic, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:42:07-07:00","id":101428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101364#post101364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're aware you're using the term &quot;realistic&quot; in the context of a fictional moral scale of fictional beings based on mythology?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're aware that not everyone is comfortable or familiar with using the word &quot;verisimilitude&quot; and its derivatives and thus that quibbling over a word whose meaning in this context is entirely understandable is incredibly needlessly pedantic, I hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T15:05:15-07:00","id":101509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101428#post101428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're aware that not everyone is comfortable or familiar with using the word &quot;verisimilitude&quot; and its derivatives and thus that quibbling over a word whose meaning in this context is entirely understandable is incredibly needlessly pedantic, I hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T15:37:39-07:00","id":101538,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Please drop the word choice argument.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T07:49:40-07:00","id":101918,"title":"","content":"Well. Something interesting happened the other day. I was talking about the new Harmony with my buddy and I brought up the fact that it will no longer need XP. This is one of my favorite things about the new Harmony. Given how it's going to work it makes sense. However, my buddy was NOT thrilled with the news. His first impression was that this was unfair to other Splats who have to spends XP to raise thier Integrity equivalent traits. He and I are very crossover minded and as such, tend to look at the BIG picture. Like I said, I think it's great. He on the other hand... I think I'm going to have some trouble trying to convince him.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:04:04-07:00","id":101931,"title":"","content":"Well, we already have different costs for the Integrity stats (Mortals and Demons vs Vampires), so this is nothing entirely new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:05:07-07:00","id":101933,"title":"","content":"Werewolves has always been an XP sink. Actually, if the rules breaking points hold true in Harmony, a werewolf should take a Beat when he's forced to make a disharmony roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:14:05-07:00","id":101937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101918#post101918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. Something interesting happened the other day. I was talking about the new Harmony with my buddy and I brought up the fact that it will no longer need XP. This is one of my favorite things about the new Harmony. Given how it's going to work it makes sense. However, my buddy was NOT thrilled with the news. His first impression was that this was unfair to other Splats who have to spends XP to raise thier Integrity equivalent traits. He and I are very crossover minded and as such, tend to look at the BIG picture. Like I said, I think it's great. He on the other hand... I think I'm going to have some trouble trying to convince him.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Other splats have the ABILITY to raise their Integrity stat with xp. Werewolves do not, they have to go through breaking points to alter it in either direction. Additionally, other splats always benefit from raising their Integrity stat. Werewolves are penalized if theirs gets too high OR to low. If anything, werewolves have a distinct disadvantage compared to other splats when it comes to their Integrity stat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:15:31-07:00","id":101938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101918#post101918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. Something interesting happened the other day. I was talking about the new Harmony with my buddy and I brought up the fact that it will no longer need XP. This is one of my favorite things about the new Harmony. Given how it's going to work it makes sense. However, my buddy was NOT thrilled with the news. His first impression was that this was unfair to other Splats who have to spends XP to raise thier Integrity equivalent traits. He and I are very crossover minded and as such, tend to look at the BIG picture. Like I said, I think it's great. He on the other hand... I think I'm going to have some trouble trying to convince him.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If he thinks that it is unfair, simply point out that Mages get Arcane Exp which is arguably more beneficial. Werewolves get a reduction in things they need to purchase, while Mages simply get free exp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T09:43:25-07:00","id":101990,"title":"","content":"Thanks, guys. All great points. I'll try and use some of these examples to help him understand. Maybe he'll come around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T20:38:27-07:00","id":102351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=101990#post101990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, guys. All great points. I'll try and use some of these examples to help him understand. Maybe he'll come around.</div> </div> </div> </div>You go do that, and while you're at it, inform him that any other splat besides Werewolf (and Promethean) have a significantly easier time with their power fuel. Werewolves can find a locus or 2, but holy hell can they be hard to hold onto sometimes. The biggest ones are large battlegrounds that require constant tending either directly, or through numerous bribes (typically Essence). When was the last time you saw a Vampire bitching that his Vitae supply was constantly under attack by beings from another world on a daily basis and the only way to counter it was by giving other people Vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T02:36:04-07:00","id":102511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=102351#post102351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When was the last time you saw a Vampire bitching that his Vitae supply was constantly under attack by beings from another world on a daily basis and the only way to counter it was by giving other people Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, but replacing &quot;beings from another world&quot; with &quot;other vampires&quot; and you've got the basic vampiric feudal power structure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T05:42:00-07:00","id":102573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=102351#post102351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You go do that, and while you're at it, inform him that any other splat besides Werewolf (and Promethean) have a significantly easier time with their power fuel. Werewolves can find a locus or 2, but holy hell can they be hard to hold onto sometimes. The biggest ones are large battlegrounds that require constant tending either directly, or through numerous bribes (typically Essence). When was the last time you saw a Vampire bitching that his Vitae supply was constantly under attack by beings from another world on a daily basis and the only way to counter it was by giving other people Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't go with this one. Vampires, mages, and lings may have an easy time with their fuel supply, but Sin Eaters and demons have as just a difficult a time as werewolves. Bound have to deal with ghosts in order to get their refills, and Unchained risk getting hunted by angels. Their Haunts and suborned Infrastructures are just as much in need of tending as a Loci.<br /> <br /> <br /> Truthfully, I've never run into a game where people have dropped exp into a Morality/Integrity equivalent, unless we're talking about a concept that revolves around being a super saint. I somehow doubt that it'll become an issue of balance between supernaturals when I'm not seeing it ever done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-31-2014, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T06:32:01-07:00","id":102597,"title":"","content":"To be fair, both Demon and B&amp;S put a lot of effort into making both affordable and relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T21:34:16-07:00","id":103144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=102597#post102597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, both Demon and B&amp;S put a lot of effort into making both affordable and relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think Changelings have it a bit too easy sometimes. Oh well<br /> <br /> One thing I am really wondering is how Werewolves will play into some core mechanics such as Abjurations or Exorcisms. Those usually require a high morality which could be very inconvenient for a balanced Werewolf. Then again...it also makes some odd twisted sort of sense that Werewolves would be bad at those things by their very nature unless they willingly abandon the spirit side.<br /> <br /> That, and I hope that Fetish activation is no longer tied to Harmony since it caused some huge issues primarily amongst the Pure tribes due to their naturally lower Harmony. I always found it odd that the Pure who have better standing amongst the spirits would by and large have a harder time using a spirit fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T23:07:03-07:00","id":103202,"title":"","content":"The preview heavily implied that Harmony would not be used for rolls precisely for those sorts of reasons. We'll probably see Harmony provide modifiers to various werewolf supernatural activities that will be rolled based on something else.<br /> <br /> So if Rituals no longer uses Harmony, but some other trait, with Harmony as a modifier, that would likely replace the Abjuration/Exorcisms rolls for mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T20:28:43-07:00","id":103806,"title":"","content":"Currently, I am imagining shapeshifting to follow the following rules<br /> <br /> 10 - Trapped in Material, instant action, Shapeshifting with essence only<br /> 9 - instant action, -5 penalty to shapeshifting rolls<br /> 8 - instant action, -3 penalty to shapeshifting rolls<br /> 7 - instant action, -1 penalty to shapeshifting rolls<br /> 6 - instant action, no penalty<br /> 5 - <b>reflexive action</b>, no penalty<br /> 4 - instant action, no penalty<br /> 3 - instant action, resolve + composure -1 to not shapeshift<br /> 2 - instant action, resolve + composure -3 to not shapeshift<br /> 1 - instant action, resolve + composure -5 to not shapeshift<br /> 0 - Trapped in shadow, <b>reflexive action</b>, essence required to not shapeshift<br /> <br /> Thoughts, guesses, concerns, pitchforks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T23:24:08-07:00","id":103867,"title":"","content":"Actually I don't think you'll see penalties at Harmony 7 or 3 for that matter, given characters are gonna start around that level. Granted, a -1 isn't much of a penalty but it'll still be a headscratcher for new, out of the gate PCs, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T08:30:11-07:00","id":104062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=103144#post103144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I am really wondering is how Werewolves will play into some core mechanics such as Abjurations or Exorcisms. Those usually require a high morality which could be very inconvenient for a balanced Werewolf. Then again...it also makes some odd twisted sort of sense that Werewolves would be bad at those things by their very nature unless they willingly abandon the spirit side.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've personally never allowed supernaturals to use exorcism or abjuration rules. Vampires have rituals, werewolves have rites, mages have rotes. They already have means of doing abjurations via their splat's magics. It should remain that way. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That, and I hope that Fetish activation is no longer tied to Harmony since it caused some huge issues primarily amongst the Pure tribes due to their naturally lower Harmony. I always found it odd that the Pure who have better standing amongst the spirits would by and large have a harder time using a spirit fetish. </div> </div> </div> That, and rites. It was always strange to me how Bale Hounds needed rites to function, and yet, their low harmony pool meant they were hideously bad at them? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T12:49:16-07:00","id":113493,"title":"","content":"So it is no longer punishable as a werewolf to kill a werewolf? (Blood Talons)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T12:54:01-07:00","id":113495,"title":"","content":"Remains to be seen.<br /> But it does seem like you are meant to go up and down in harmony dots, so until you hit the far end either way you're good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T13:08:16-07:00","id":113503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=113493#post113493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is no longer punishable as a werewolf to kill a werewolf? (Blood Talons)</div> </div> </div> </div>I really, truly, seriously doubt that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:44:37-07:00","id":113736,"title":"","content":"The thing with this approach to Harmony is that, doesn't matters that there's a sin for this or a sin for that, you can just sin in the opposite direction to balance out. Even maybe indulge in controlled cannibalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:53:01-07:00","id":113740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=113736#post113736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with this approach to Harmony is that, doesn't matters that there's a sin for this or a sin for that, you can just sin in the opposite direction to balance out. Even maybe indulge in controlled cannibalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one would love it if this was possible to an extent. In order to actively swing Harmony one way or another I can't simply let my players say &quot;ok, if I cannibalize this werewolf, I will simply donate to a church to balance it out.&quot; This is very different than doing the exact same thing in a roleplay perspective due to feeling guilt about what you just did. It is all how the player approaches the situation that determines the result. Otherwise I will call shenanigans on rule manipulation and breach of the 4th wall and disallow it.<br /> <br /> Still, assuming we are all dedicated roleplayers here, simply knowing that if my character gives in to Kuruth and eats another werewolf for essence, it makes me feel much better knowing that I am not on a 1 way trip to unplayable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:24:20-07:00","id":114085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=113740#post113740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I for one would love it if this was possible to an extent. In order to actively swing Harmony one way or another I can't simply let my players say &amp;quot;ok, if I cannibalize this werewolf, I will simply donate to a church to balance it out.&amp;quot; This is very different than doing the exact same thing in a roleplay perspective due to feeling guilt about what you just did. It is all how the player approaches the situation that determines the result. Otherwise I will call shenanigans on rule manipulation and breach of the 4th wall and disallow it. Still, assuming we are all dedicated roleplayers here, simply knowing that if my character gives in to Kuruth and eats another werewolf for essence, it makes me feel much better knowing that I am not on a 1 way trip to unplayable.</div> </div> </div> </div> Also, from the way the blog made it sound, Breaking Points towards Spirit are things that characters are just naturally going to end up doing, because they're Werewolves (I assume killing another Werewolf will be on this side of the scale, as killing the Pure is pretty common for Uratha to do and vice versa). Whereas Breaking Points towards Human will be things you have to make a conscious effort to do. So I imagine it'll be less like &quot;Kill an Ivory Claw, donate to a church to balance it out&quot; and more like &quot;Kill an Ivory Claw, go pay a visit to your touchstone to get yourself re-grounded in normal human behavior.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:58:31-07:00","id":114109,"title":"","content":"I guess I may have stated my feelings on the topic a bit poorly. My issue isn't having a touchstone to keep yourself grounded since that is perfectly acceptable. My issue is players making a conscious 4th wall decision that the harmony hit they are about to take can just be erased afterwards by interaction with their touchstone. In a sense, thinking the upcoming consequences do not matter since they can just fix it afterwards with no real effort.<br /> <br /> For the touchstone to be effective, there must also be a conscious roleplay element to the interaction beyond &quot;I visit my touchstone.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't want to see touchstones used as a crutch, but more as a key roleplay element to keep you grounded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T11:15:34-07:00","id":114207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=114109#post114109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I may have stated my feelings on the topic a bit poorly. My issue isn't having a touchstone to keep yourself grounded since that is perfectly acceptable. My issue is players making a conscious 4th wall decision that the harmony hit they are about to take can just be erased afterwards by interaction with their touchstone. In a sense, thinking the upcoming consequences do not matter since they can just fix it afterwards with no real effort. For the touchstone to be effective, there must also be a conscious roleplay element to the interaction beyond &amp;quot;I visit my touchstone.&amp;quot; I don't want to see touchstones used as a crutch, but more as a key roleplay element to keep you grounded.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. I more meant that it sounds like the mechanics are being designed to work around that by making it easy to hit Spirit Breaking Points by accident, and difficult to hit Human Breaking Points and requiring you to set out to intentionally hit them. So they'll naturally skew more towards Spirit faster, and &quot;fixing&quot; it will require going through the ST. I mean, there will always be players that try to game any system like this (I remember a lot of this sort if behavior from &quot;true neutral&quot; characters in D&amp;D, for example), but it seems to me the system is being built with the intention of not being as easy to game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T12:08:50-07:00","id":114240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=114109#post114109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I may have stated my feelings on the topic a bit poorly. My issue isn't having a touchstone to keep yourself grounded since that is perfectly acceptable. My issue is players making a conscious 4th wall decision that the harmony hit they are about to take can just be erased afterwards by interaction with their touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, I don't think it's going to be a 4th wall decision. I don't think the Uratha will be completely oblivious to their harmony. They won't be able to say &quot;I'm at Harmony 4&quot;, but they will be able to notice when they had perfect Harmony, and slipped, and be able to consciously re-attain that balance.<br /> <br /> And you know what happens when a PC goes &quot;I should go visit my touchstone&quot;? That's when the ST deliberately endangers it. By the very PC or by external threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T13:30:24-07:00","id":115505,"title":"","content":"Yeah I can see that as an IC decision. &quot;I'm planning on killing some Pure on this outing. I need to set up some time with my wife afterwards because she helps keep me grounded&quot; is the IC translation of &quot;I'm about to risk Harmony, character's wife is his Touchstone to the flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T14:47:15-07:00","id":120553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=98162#post98162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lota... Lota piracy going on on that site you linked to there...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of piracy on any website that lets you share stuff. I personally like 4shared because it's easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T20:07:11-07:00","id":120689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xaielao</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/96423-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-harmony?p=120553#post120553\" rel=\"no